WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.580 --> 00:00:04.980
Less than a month after it was reported that
Academy Award-nominated actor Jonah Hill was

00:00:04.980 --> 00:00:09.760
lined up to star alongside Robert Pattinson
in The Batman, Deadline has dropped a bombshell:

00:00:09.860 --> 00:00:11.820
Hill is no longer in talks for the movie.

00:00:12.140 --> 00:00:16.180
Hill, originally known for roles in raunchy
comedies, took his career to new heights with

00:00:16.180 --> 00:00:20.620
his astounding performances in The Wolf of
Wall Street and the Netflix series Maniac,

00:00:20.620 --> 00:00:24.380
was reportedly being courted to portray a
villain in the Matt Reeves-directed film.

00:00:24.480 --> 00:00:29.019
Though Warner Bros. gave no explicit confirmation,
outlets widely claimed that Hill would play

00:00:29.020 --> 00:00:32.380
either the Riddler or Penguin opposite Pattinson's
Bruce Wayne.

00:00:32.600 --> 00:00:36.810
Sources close to Deadline with knowledge of
the situation have indicated that talks broke

00:00:36.810 --> 00:00:39.920
down between Hill and the powers that be at
Warner Bros.

00:00:40.020 --> 00:00:42.460
But why exactly did those conversations stop?

00:00:42.780 --> 00:00:46.880
It's looking like the split was a mutual decision,
and it may have at least partially been over

00:00:46.880 --> 00:00:47.380
money.

00:00:47.440 --> 00:00:51.480
Per The Hollywood Reporter, Hill and Warner
Bros. simply couldn't, quote, "come to terms

00:00:51.480 --> 00:00:56.190
on a deal" language that hints that contractual
negotiations may have been the meat of the

00:00:56.190 --> 00:00:58.280
talks between the actor and the studio.

00:00:58.440 --> 00:01:02.400
Hill passing on The Batman, or Warner Bros.
executives telling him things just weren't

00:01:02.400 --> 00:01:05.320
going to work out, may actually have been
weeks in the making.

00:01:05.320 --> 00:01:11.460
Variety reporter Justin Kroll indicated in
a now-deleted tweet on September 25, 2019

00:01:11.460 --> 00:01:15.330
exactly three weeks before Deadline's new
report that Hill was sitting on the offer

00:01:15.330 --> 00:01:19.900
for The Batman "for over a month" and that
money was a "bargaining point" in conversations

00:01:19.900 --> 00:01:20.880
with Warner Bros.

00:01:20.980 --> 00:01:26.380
According to Kroll's sources, Hill reportedly
wanted $10 million more than double what Pattinson

00:01:26.380 --> 00:01:28.340
is making for actually leading the film.

00:01:28.560 --> 00:01:30.340
"Uh, don't forget about my money."

00:01:30.740 --> 00:01:34.900
These claims haven't been corroborated, but
this wasn't coming from some rumor site.

00:01:34.900 --> 00:01:35.620
It's Variety.

00:01:35.940 --> 00:01:39.880
Kroll also noted that Hill and Warner Bros.
may have been torn between the two roles,

00:01:39.880 --> 00:01:43.980
unable to decide whether he'd star as the
Riddler or Penguin, but it seems more likely

00:01:43.980 --> 00:01:46.190
that money was the biggest motivating factor.

00:01:46.520 --> 00:01:48.940
"If you're good at something, never do it
for free."

00:01:49.380 --> 00:01:53.000
Even without Hill, The Batman has some serious
star power attached to it.

00:01:53.140 --> 00:01:57.670
Reeves, who's known for directing the original
Cloverfield, the horror remake Let Me In,

00:01:57.670 --> 00:02:01.260
and the sequels Dawn of the Planet of the
Apes and War for the Planet of the Apes, is

00:02:01.260 --> 00:02:01.860
at the helm.

00:02:02.040 --> 00:02:06.120
Pattinson, who has become something of an
indie movie king and has long since shed the

00:02:06.120 --> 00:02:10.040
weight of his breakout role in the Twilight
film franchise, is the title star.

00:02:10.250 --> 00:02:14.560
Jeffrey Wright will play Commissioner Gordon
and newly added actress Zoë Kravitz will

00:02:14.560 --> 00:02:16.220
dig her claws into Catwoman.

00:02:16.380 --> 00:02:20.900
Even without Hill on board, The Batman is
packing major heat, and Warner Bros. is already

00:02:20.900 --> 00:02:25.040
looking to find someone just as talented as
Hill to add even further star power.

00:02:25.270 --> 00:02:29.000
The studio is said to now be looking at new
candidates to portray either the Riddler or

00:02:29.000 --> 00:02:33.220
Penguin in The Batman, and as for who those
lucky actors might be, there have been some

00:02:33.220 --> 00:02:37.840
rumblings about Seth Rogen another funny guy
often linked to Hill, who has been breaking

00:02:37.840 --> 00:02:41.330
ever more into fresher territory potentially
stepping up.

00:02:41.330 --> 00:02:44.690
However, Deadline notes that there was only
ever interest in Rogen for one of the two

00:02:44.690 --> 00:02:47.480
roles, with no offers or talks yet occurring.

00:02:47.670 --> 00:02:52.160
If Warner Bros. executives had their sights
set on Hill for either of the two iconic DC

00:02:52.170 --> 00:02:55.849
Comics villains, then it stands to reason
that the studio will probably go with someone

00:02:55.849 --> 00:03:01.170
else like him: a comedic actor who has proven
capable of bringing nuanced, delightful performances

00:03:01.170 --> 00:03:02.300
to more dramatic fare.

00:03:02.560 --> 00:03:03.920
And he can also be threatening:

00:03:04.680 --> 00:03:05.180
"Bang bang!"

00:03:05.180 --> 00:03:05.800
"Jesus!

00:03:05.810 --> 00:03:06.920
Please put it down!"

00:03:06.920 --> 00:03:07.420
"Oh f---!"

00:03:07.420 --> 00:03:08.100
"Bang!

00:03:08.100 --> 00:03:08.600
Bang!

00:03:08.600 --> 00:03:09.100
Bang!

00:03:09.120 --> 00:03:09.640
You're dead!"

00:03:10.080 --> 00:03:14.100
It seems that's a trend with the Batman casting,
going with an unexpected choice for a major

00:03:14.100 --> 00:03:14.600
role.

00:03:14.640 --> 00:03:19.020
Pattinson wasn't an obvious pick for Batman,
and neither was Hill for the Riddler or Penguin.

00:03:19.020 --> 00:03:22.440
Wright may also have been a surprise pick
for some as Commissioner Gordon.

00:03:22.640 --> 00:03:26.960
And though Kravitz has played Catwoman before,
voicing the antiheroine in The Lego Batman

00:03:26.960 --> 00:03:27.460
Movie...

00:03:27.460 --> 00:03:28.460
"Catwoman!"

00:03:28.540 --> 00:03:29.040
"Meow meow, you're in!

00:03:29.040 --> 00:03:29.540
Meow Meow."

00:03:29.720 --> 00:03:32.200
...her casting likewise raised some eyebrows.

00:03:32.460 --> 00:03:37.120
In related news, Warner Bros. has cast Paul
Dano as The Riddler alongside Pattinson's

00:03:37.120 --> 00:03:39.460
Batman, according to The Hollywood Reporter.

00:03:39.960 --> 00:03:43.900
You might recognize Dano from his stellar
accolades in movies like There Will Be Blood,

00:03:43.900 --> 00:03:46.800
12 Years a Slave, Prisoners, and Swiss Army
Man.

00:03:47.220 --> 00:03:52.200
The Batman will crusade into theaters without
Jonah Hill on June 25, 2021.

